(COURSE GUIDE: PROGRAMMING FOUNDATIONS) Tj
T*
(PrepWise Synthetic Demo Material - Unit 1: Variables and Expressions) Tj
T*
(==================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.1 Memory Model and Assignment Semantics) Tj
T*
(In Python, an assignment statement does not copy memory bytes. Instead,) Tj
T*
(it binds a variable name to an object reference in memory.) Tj
T*
(Example:) Tj
T*
(    count = 10) Tj
T*
(    total = count) Tj
T*
(Both 'count' and 'total' now point to the integer object 10.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.2 Dynamic Typing and Primitive Types) Tj
T*
(Variables do not have fixed static types; values do. The primary types are:) Tj
T*
(- int: Arbitrary precision signed integers \(e.g., -5, 0, 1024\).) Tj
T*
(- float: Double-precision floating point numbers \(e.g., 3.14159\).) Tj
T*
(- bool: True or False \(subclass of int, where True == 1\).) Tj
T*
(- str: Immutable Unicode character sequences.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.3 Arithmetic Expressions and Precedence) Tj
T*
(Operators follow standard precedence: PEMDAS \(Parentheses, Exponents **, ) Tj
T*
(Multiplication/Division *, /, //, %, Addition/Subtraction +, -\).) Tj
T*
(Integer division \(//\) truncates toward negative infinity.) Tj
T*
