(COURSE GUIDE: PROGRAMMING FOUNDATIONS) Tj
T*
(PrepWise Synthetic Demo Material - Unit 2: Conditional Logic) Tj
T*
(===========================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.1 Truthiness and Boolean Evaluation) Tj
T*
(Every Python value has an implicit boolean value in a conditional context:) Tj
T*
(- Falsy values: False, None, 0, 0.0, '', [], \(\), {}.) Tj
T*
(- Truthy values: Any non-zero number, non-empty string, or collection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.2 Comparison Operators and Chaining) Tj
T*
(Comparisons include == \(equality\), != \(inequality\), <, <=, >, >=.) Tj
T*
(Python supports chained comparisons: 0 <= score <= 100 is equivalent to) Tj
T*
(\(0 <= score\) and \(score <= 100\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.3 Multi-Way Branching Structure) Tj
T*
(The if-elif-else construct evaluates clauses sequentially from top to bottom.) Tj
T*
(As soon as one branch guard evaluates to True, its block executes and) Tj
T*
(all subsequent branches are skipped.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.4 Short-Circuit Evaluation) Tj
T*
(Logical operators 'and' and 'or' evaluate operands lazily from left to right.) Tj
T*
(In 'A and B', if A is False, B is never evaluated.) Tj
T*
(In 'A or B', if A is True, B is never evaluated.) Tj
T*
