(COURSE GUIDE: PROGRAMMING FOUNDATIONS) Tj
T*
(PrepWise Synthetic Demo Material - Unit 3: Loops and Iteration Bounds) Tj
T*
(=====================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.1 While-Loop Invariants and Guard Conditions) Tj
T*
(A while loop repeats its indented body as long as the condition remains True.) Tj
T*
(The condition is checked at the entry of each iteration, not continuously.) Tj
T*
(Syntax:) Tj
T*
(    while condition:) Tj
T*
(        # loop body must update state to eventually falsify condition) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 Sentinel Values and Termination Guarantees) Tj
T*
(To prevent infinite loops, ensure that loop control variables make monotonic) Tj
T*
(progress toward a termination boundary on every iteration path.) Tj
T*
(Example of proper boundary check:) Tj
T*
(    idx = 0) Tj
T*
(    while idx < len\(items\):) Tj
T*
(        process\(items[idx]\)) Tj
T*
(        idx += 1  # Guaranteed progress) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3 Loop Control: break and continue) Tj
T*
(- break: Terminates the innermost loop immediately.) Tj
T*
(- continue: Skips remainder of current iteration and jumps to guard evaluation.) Tj
T*
ET
