(COURSE GUIDE: PROGRAMMING FOUNDATIONS) Tj
T*
(PrepWise Synthetic Demo Material - Unit 4: The Accumulator Pattern) Tj
T*
(=================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1 Anatomical Structure of an Accumulator) Tj
T*
(An accumulator pattern aggregates data across multiple loop iterations.) Tj
T*
(It consists of three mandatory elements:) Tj
T*
(1. Initialization: Set the accumulator variable BEFORE the loop starts.) Tj
T*
(2. Update: Modify the accumulator inside the loop body using incoming items.) Tj
T*
(3. Result: Read the accumulated value AFTER the loop completes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Summation vs Multiplicative Accumulators) Tj
T*
(- Sum accumulator must be initialized to the additive identity: 0.) Tj
T*
(    total = 0) Tj
T*
(    for x in numbers: total += x) Tj
T*
(- Product accumulator must be initialized to multiplicative identity: 1.) Tj
T*
(    product = 1) Tj
T*
(    for x in factors: product *= x) Tj
T*
(\(Warning: initializing product to 0 is a fatal zero-product bug!\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 Filtering Accumulators) Tj
T*
(Combines conditional statements inside the loop to accumulate only matches.) Tj
T*
(    evens = []) Tj
T*
(    for num in values:) Tj
T*
(        if num % 2 == 0:) Tj
T*
(            evens.append\(num\)) Tj
T*
ET
